   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
    "Print", "[", "\"\<In Case 6D_2, the curled \!\(\*SuperscriptBox[\(S\), \
\(2\)]\) does pinch to a point at \!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(r\), \
\(0\)]\)=\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(p\), \(4\)]\), as in a KK bubble, \nbut no \
smoothness condition is needed: \n\[Bullet] In order for \
\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(\[GothicCapitalD]\), \(4\)]\)(r) \[GreaterEqual] 0, we \
must have r\.b2 \[LessEqual] \!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(p\), \(4\)]\)\.b2, or 0 \
\[LessEqual] r \[LessEqual] \!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(p\), \(4\)]\). \n\[Bullet] \
The \\\"pinch\\\" candidate would be \!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(r\), \(0\)]\) = \
\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(p\), \(4\)]\):\n    \[Checkmark] The domain of r is \
restricted to 0 \[LessEqual] r < r0 \n    \[Checkmark] The radial line \
element for this solution is\n\t    ds\.b2 = \!\(\*FractionBox[\(1\), \
\(\(\*SubscriptBox[\(\[GothicCapitalD]\), \(4\)]\)[r]\)]\) dr\.b2 + \
\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(\[GothicCapitalD]\), \(4\)]\)[r] \
\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(p\), \(4\)]\)\.b2 [\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(d\[Psi]\), \
\(4\)]\)\.b2 + Sin[\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(\[Psi]\), \(4\)]\)]\.b2 \
\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(d\[Psi]\), \(5\)]\)\.b2]\n    \[Checkmark] As r\
\[RightArrow]r0\n\t  \[EmptySmallCircle] B\[RightArrow]\[Infinity] and \
\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(\[GothicCapitalD]\), \(4\)]\)\[RightArrow]0\n\t  \
\[EmptySmallCircle] The whole(\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(\[Psi]\), \
\(4\)]\),\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(\[Psi]\), \(5\)]\)) two-sphere shrinks from a \
sphere of radius\n\t\t\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(p\), \(4\)]\) smoothly down to \
sphere of radius zero, a single point \n\t  \[EmptySmallCircle] The 'bubble' \
closes up automatically without needing any \n\t\tconstraints \n\nThere is no \
KK-bubble constraint on \!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(p\), \(4\)]\). It remains a free \
modulus\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\n", 
