Cell[BoxData["\<\"Options (2) and (3) arise because the prior patterns have \
been based on circles (\\!\\(\\*SuperscriptBox[\\(S\\), \\(1\\)]\\)) and now \
the curled object is a sphere. This suggests that either \[CapitalBeta] = \\!\
\\(\\*FractionBox[\\(1\\), \
SuperscriptBox[SubscriptBox[\\(\[GothicCapitalD]\\), \\(4\\)], \\(2\\)]]\\) \
(option 2) or \\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(\[GothicCapitalD]\\), \\(4\\)]\\) = \
\\!\\(\\*FractionBox[\\(1\\), SuperscriptBox[\\(\[CapitalBeta]\\), \
\\(2\\)]]\\) (option 3) may be a good choice.\"\>"], "Print",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.999436845325746*^9, 3.9994390382636223`*^9, 
